## Machine runs and structured data

| Record | Sessions | Where to look |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Chat files | 44 | Readable transcripts above, each beside its JSON |
| Subagents | 464 | [Session index](index.json) → named bundle and member |
| CLI runs | 2,650 | [Session index](index.json) → named bundle and member |
| Archive-only sessions | 29 | Preserved records whose native session metadata is no longer available |

The 44 chat files contain 372 user-channel messages. Inherited prompts and AI-dispatched task packets are not counted as new human contributions. The 29 archive-only sessions add 58 saved messages that the earlier export missed.

The [bundle manifest](bundles/manifest.json) lists every archive, member path, byte count, and SHA-256. The session index identifies the current conversation and any separate turn-metadata bundle. Earlier snapshots remain available.

Download the named bundle and extract it into a separate directory:

```sh
tar -xzf <bundle>.tar.gz
```

<a id="claude-after-the-midterm"></a>

## Claude

The [Claude index](claude/index.json) retains 63 cumulative launcher collections, 4,824 distinct collection records, 65 observed CLI session IDs, and 5 legacy bridge jobs. Repeated snapshots are not additional model calls.

The direct post-midterm branch also retains five conversations: [search](claude/direct/search-RS-R01/conversation.md), [C2 critique](claude/direct/critic-PCR-C2/conversation.md), [C5 critique](claude/direct/critic-PCR-C5/conversation.md), [C2 repair](claude/direct/repair-PCR-C2/conversation.md), and [C5 repair](claude/direct/repair-PCR-C5/conversation.md).

<a id="coverage-and-dates"></a>

## Preservation and coverage

This edition adds 129 visible messages. All 13,751 previously exported Codex message objects survive unchanged, and all 26 earlier bundle files retain their exact bytes. Replaced readable files and indexes are kept in the history bundles. The [preservation check](snapshots/20261017-editorial-verification.json) verifies all bundle members. The [snapshot receipt](snapshots/20261017-editorial-02.json) records the cutoffs and the correction for compressed native files.

Coverage ends at fixed per-session cutoffs; this snapshot began at `2026-10-17T22:53:22.689946+00:00`. The current index lists 118 capture items: 94 tool-schema items, 13 oversized or incomplete records, and 11 attachment or event-format items. Missing native files keep their previously saved records. Hidden reasoning, internal instructions, credentials, unreviewed tool bodies, and unsupported attachments are outside this visible-record export.

All retained Codex messages have source timestamps. Dates shown to readers use America/Los_Angeles; message time, capture time, release time, and export time remain distinct. Observed settings and wall time are stored when available; wall time includes tools and waiting.
